814
01:06:14,000 --> 01:06:15,240
What am I supposed to do?

815
01:06:15,760 --> 01:06:16,840
I have made a commitment.

816
01:06:17,320 --> 01:06:19,080
Build up something else.

817
01:06:20,240 --> 01:06:22,480
You've got more to offer
than those morons.

818
01:06:28,000 --> 01:06:30,720
Hey, they are my friends.
You don't even know them.

819
01:06:31,320 --> 01:06:32,240
Then go.

820
01:06:34,120 --> 01:06:35,320
- Go!
- Edith...

821
01:06:35,480 --> 01:06:37,640
No leave, I want to be alone anyway.

822
01:06:43,840 --> 01:06:45,840
- Even a really old picture.
- Grinsi...

823
01:06:46,000 --> 01:06:48,160
- Don't you spot something like that?
- Well, I...

824
01:06:48,320 --> 01:06:49,400
Look at this thing.

825
01:06:49,800 --> 01:06:51,120
Wow, can I see?

826
01:06:51,560 --> 01:06:53,320
- Oh, that's really heavy.
- Hey.

827
01:06:53,480 --> 01:06:54,400
Let me see.

828
01:06:57,640 --> 01:06:59,640
- Are you a couple now?
- With whom?

829
01:07:00,080 --> 01:07:02,400
- With that Schwartz girl.
- Seems to pay off.

830
01:07:03,280 --> 01:07:04,440
What are you trying to say?

831
01:07:04,600 --> 01:07:05,520
Nothing.

832
01:07:06,440 --> 01:07:07,720
I bought it myself.

833
01:07:07,880 --> 01:07:09,680
Mhm.
And the picture?

834
01:07:11,080 --> 01:07:12,360
That was a stupid bet.

835
01:07:12,520 --> 01:07:13,440
Hm.

836
01:07:13,800 --> 01:07:14,720
No chatting.

837
01:07:15,360 --> 01:07:16,680
Continue.

838
01:07:24,280 --> 01:07:26,120
When did you stop telling me things?

839
01:07:26,680 --> 01:07:27,600
Nasic?

840
01:07:28,640 --> 01:07:30,000
There's a lot going on right now.

841
01:07:30,160 --> 01:07:31,080
Mhm.

842
01:07:31,720 --> 01:07:32,960
Are you coming tonight?

843
01:07:34,000 --> 01:07:34,960
Yes, of course.

844
01:07:36,840 --> 01:07:38,560
Why don't you bring Edith?

845
01:07:39,880 --> 01:07:42,240
I don't think that she is
into stuff like that.

846
01:07:54,440 --> 01:07:55,360
Hey!

847
01:07:59,640 --> 01:08:00,560
Yeah?

848
01:08:05,960 --> 01:08:06,920
Come with me.

849
01:08:31,360 --> 01:08:33,480
Why do you think I am
against this therapy?

850
01:08:34,400 --> 01:08:37,080
- We were informed about the risks.
- Really?

851
01:08:37,240 --> 01:08:40,720
So tell me, which stem cells do
they use for the oligodendrocytes?

852
01:08:41,000 --> 01:08:41,960
Do you know that?

853
01:08:42,440 --> 01:08:44,200
I don't know that right now.

854
01:08:44,360 --> 01:08:47,920
Do you know how high the tumour risk is
with such an allogeneic transplant?

855
01:08:48,080 --> 01:08:49,560
You're pushing Edith into such
a therapy and you

856
01:08:49,720 --> 01:08:51,800
and you haven't even properly
informed yourself?

857
01:08:55,600 --> 01:08:56,960
You don't know Edith.

858
01:08:57,280 --> 01:08:59,920
You have to protect her from
herself sometimes.

859
01:09:01,880 --> 01:09:04,080
You're underestimating
Edith right now.

860
01:09:07,920 --> 01:09:08,840
Dad?

861
01:09:12,360 --> 01:09:13,320
Dad!

862
01:09:15,720 --> 01:09:16,640
Hey.

863
01:09:17,160 --> 01:09:18,080
Hey.

864
01:09:23,920 --> 01:09:25,360
What happened?

865
01:09:26,040 --> 01:09:28,560
I lost my balance somehow.

866
01:09:33,200 --> 01:09:34,680
Can you help me?

867
01:09:35,800 --> 01:09:36,720
Yes, of course.

868
01:09:37,560 --> 01:09:39,320
- How?
- Here.

869
01:09:50,360 --> 01:09:51,680
Have you been sick again?

870
01:09:52,240 --> 01:09:53,480
I'm fine again.

871
01:09:54,600 --> 01:09:56,280
Can you pass me the bathrobe?

872
01:09:56,440 --> 01:09:57,360
Sure.

873
01:10:20,040 --> 01:10:22,080
Do you really want to go
through with this?

874
01:10:22,600 --> 01:10:23,520
What?

875
01:10:24,920 --> 01:10:26,200
Well, with the therapy.

876
01:10:29,320 --> 01:10:32,200
What's a bit of vomiting if I
could walk again.

877
01:10:33,480 --> 01:10:35,000
Well that's not all.

878
01:10:35,600 --> 01:10:36,960
Are you backing out?

879
01:10:37,840 --> 01:10:38,840
No.

880
01:10:39,000 --> 01:10:40,840
I thought you were on my side.

881
01:10:41,000 --> 01:10:41,920
I am.

882
01:10:53,800 --> 01:10:55,360
Are you ashamed of me?

883
01:10:56,120 --> 01:10:57,600
What the fuck is that about?

884
01:10:58,320 --> 01:11:01,000
Then why don't you take me to Holzers?

885
01:11:01,480 --> 01:11:03,000
Why?
Do you want to?

886
01:11:03,800 --> 01:11:04,720
No.

887
01:11:05,240 --> 01:11:07,200
But I want you to ask me.

888
01:11:13,040 --> 01:11:13,960
Oh.

889
01:11:16,120 --> 01:11:17,560
Alright... Prosecco?

890
01:11:18,440 --> 01:11:19,480
I'm not allowed right now.

891
01:11:19,640 --> 01:11:20,560
Thank you.

892
01:11:20,840 --> 01:11:21,800
Oh God.

893
01:11:21,960 --> 01:11:24,520
How are you going to put up
with it here then?

894
01:11:24,680 --> 01:11:25,640
Nasic!

895
01:11:26,600 --> 01:11:27,680
Come on, line up.

896
01:11:28,320 --> 01:11:30,480
- Look what you're doing!
- Come on now!

897
01:11:31,600 --> 01:11:32,520
Hey.

898
01:11:33,240 --> 01:11:34,240
You little guy.

899
01:11:34,400 --> 01:11:36,080
Mum, TV.

900
01:11:37,600 --> 01:11:39,440
Excuse me?
I didn't understand you.

901
01:11:39,600 --> 01:11:42,520
Dear mum, can you please turn on
the TV for me, please?

902
01:11:42,680 --> 01:11:43,600
I'll be right there.

903
01:11:44,800 --> 01:11:45,960
He is so sweet.

904
01:11:46,720 --> 01:11:47,880
A little devil.

905
01:11:48,280 --> 01:11:50,400
But he can be quite sweet
when he wants to be.

906
01:11:50,760 --> 01:11:52,360
I used to work for your father.

907
01:11:52,520 --> 01:11:53,440
Oh.

908
01:11:54,160 --> 01:11:55,400
That's not what I meant.

909
01:11:55,680 --> 01:11:56,640
Don't worry.

910
01:11:57,280 --> 01:11:58,200
Mum!

911
01:11:59,920 --> 01:12:02,960
I'll be right back.
Otherwise we'll never have any peace.

912
01:12:16,280 --> 01:12:17,280
Oh, sorry.

913
01:13:55,480 --> 01:13:58,160
Why are you always
sitting in that chair?

914
01:13:58,720 --> 01:14:00,600
Because my legs are broken.

915
01:14:01,280 --> 01:14:02,240
Why?

916
01:14:03,000 --> 01:14:04,800
Because I had an accident.

917
01:14:05,160 --> 01:14:06,080
Why?

918
01:14:06,360 --> 01:14:08,320
Because someone wasn't
paying attention.

919
01:14:11,680 --> 01:14:13,120
Are you sad?

920
01:14:13,400 --> 01:14:14,480
Sometimes.

921
01:14:16,240 --> 01:14:17,920
Do you want to watch with me?

922
01:14:20,400 --> 01:14:21,400
I'd love to.

923
01:14:21,960 --> 01:14:22,880
Tommy.

924
01:14:25,480 --> 01:14:26,640
Go to your mum.

925
01:14:26,800 --> 01:14:27,720
It's okay.

926
01:14:28,200 --> 01:14:30,920
- But I've only just started.
- Go.

927
01:14:31,400 --> 01:14:32,320
No!

928
01:14:32,720 --> 01:14:34,200
It's really okay.

929
01:14:35,920 --> 01:14:37,360
Or I'll turn it off.

930
01:14:47,000 --> 01:14:47,920
I'm sorry.

931
01:14:51,240 --> 01:14:53,840
It's okay.
He's such a sweet boy.

932
01:14:56,160 --> 01:14:58,200
Are we not good enough for you?

933
01:14:59,480 --> 01:15:00,600
Not at all.

934
01:15:02,320 --> 01:15:04,480
- I wanted...
- Holzer!

935
01:15:05,040 --> 01:15:06,800
1,2,3,4.

936
01:15:07,120 --> 01:15:10,960
<i>Today we want to march.</i>

937
01:15:11,240 --> 01:15:14,640
<i>Try a new march.</i>

938
01:15:15,320 --> 01:15:18,440
<i>In the beautiful Westerwald.</i>

939
01:15:18,600 --> 01:15:21,640
<i>Where the wind whistles so cold.</i>

940
01:15:21,960 --> 01:15:22,920
Holzer!

941
01:15:23,080 --> 01:15:28,720
<i>Oh, you beautiful Westerwald.</i>

942
01:15:29,200 --> 01:15:30,360
Eucalyptus candy!

943
01:15:30,520 --> 01:15:33,520
<i>The wind whistles so cold
over your caves.</i>

944
01:15:33,960 --> 01:15:37,560
<i>However, the smallest sunshine</i>

945
01:15:37,720 --> 01:15:40,440
<i>goes deep into your heart.</i>

946
01:15:40,600 --> 01:15:41,800
Yes!

947
01:15:43,120 --> 01:15:44,120
Thank you.

948
01:15:44,280 --> 01:15:45,960
Thank you, you fuckers.

949
01:15:46,120 --> 01:15:47,840
Holzer old bastard, make a speech!

950
01:15:48,640 --> 01:15:51,560
We even have a star guest
among us today.

951
01:15:51,960 --> 01:15:53,720
A real Schwartz.

952
01:15:54,000 --> 01:15:57,200
I am honoured that a real Schwartz
is here with us today.

953
01:15:57,360 --> 01:15:58,520
Let's hear it!

954
01:16:04,840 --> 01:16:08,760
- He doesn't mean it in a bad way.
- Yes, and she also brought her nurse.

955
01:16:09,680 --> 01:16:11,520
So thank you for

956
01:16:11,680 --> 01:16:13,920
having made it all the way to my
modest little hut.

957
01:16:14,080 --> 01:16:17,040
- Now, the important things.
- Hey!

958
01:16:19,080 --> 01:16:20,000
Hey!

959
01:16:21,200 --> 01:16:23,720
- What the fuck?
- Apologize to her now.

960
01:16:24,080 --> 01:16:25,520
Right now. Apologize to her!

961
01:16:25,680 --> 01:16:26,800
It was just a joke.

962
01:16:26,960 --> 01:16:27,880
Immediately!

963
01:16:28,600 --> 01:16:31,040
You apologize to her.
Immediately!

964
01:16:31,600 --> 01:16:32,800
It was really just a joke.

965
01:16:32,960 --> 01:16:34,160
Shut up!

966
01:16:48,640 --> 01:16:50,440
What kind of people are you?

967
01:16:51,120 --> 01:16:54,120
Do you think it's normal to punch
someone in the face like that?

968
01:16:54,520 --> 01:16:56,000
What was I supposed to do?

969
01:16:56,280 --> 01:16:58,560
Just look the other way, or what?

970
01:16:58,720 --> 01:17:00,400
You shouldn't drink.

971
01:17:01,560 --> 01:17:03,440
I don't recognize you anymore.

972
01:17:09,200 --> 01:17:10,120
Sorry.

973
01:17:14,840 --> 01:17:16,760
What's going on in here?

974
01:17:19,880 --> 01:17:21,080
I know.

975
01:17:33,120 --> 01:17:34,600
I want to be better for you.

976
01:17:37,480 --> 01:17:39,720
Are you working late again tomorrow?

977
01:17:40,400 --> 01:17:41,320
Why?

978
01:17:44,520 --> 01:17:46,560
Tomorrow is the second
round in Poland.

979
01:17:46,720 --> 01:17:47,840
That's already tomorrow?

980
01:17:48,760 --> 01:17:49,680
It's okay.

981
01:17:50,080 --> 01:17:52,400
- Ilona will drive me.
- No, no, no. I'll do that.

982
01:17:53,120 --> 01:17:54,200
I'll drive you.

983
01:18:02,840 --> 01:18:04,080
You're still not done.

984
01:18:04,840 --> 01:18:06,560
How stupid can one actually be?

985
01:18:06,720 --> 01:18:09,200
Is Private Holzer supposed to
help you or what?

986
01:18:11,080 --> 01:18:14,360
Tell me, what did you actually
learn in kindergarten?

987
01:18:14,840 --> 01:18:16,640
Is that supposed to be
refined motor skills?

988
01:18:17,840 --> 01:18:20,200
I don't want to know what a mess
it is when you pee!

989
01:18:20,360 --> 01:18:22,520
- Don't shout at me.
- What?!

990
01:18:26,320 --> 01:18:28,120
Please don't shout at me.

991
01:18:35,160 --> 01:18:38,000
Do you think you can ask everyone to
be quiet on the battle field

992
01:18:38,160 --> 01:18:40,240
so that you can assemble
your rifle in peace?

993
01:18:40,400 --> 01:18:43,080
The guard battalion does not
fight in any battle.

994
01:18:44,360 --> 01:18:45,960
A real smart ass...

995
01:18:47,240 --> 01:18:48,760
The whole unit. Up!

996
01:18:52,160 --> 01:18:53,840
Get down!
Push-ups!

997
01:18:55,280 --> 01:18:56,360
Not you Nasic.

998
01:18:56,960 --> 01:18:59,000
You will assemble your
fucking rifle now.

999
01:18:59,360 --> 01:19:00,720
Everyone else. Go!

1000
01:20:33,760 --> 01:20:34,680
Hey.

1001
01:20:34,840 --> 01:20:36,480
- What's wrong?
- Everything is okay.

1002
01:20:36,640 --> 01:20:38,720
- That doesn't sound good at all.
- That's normal.

1003
01:20:38,880 --> 01:20:40,280
- How is that normal?
- Wait, wait.

1004
01:20:40,440 --> 01:20:41,440
She wants to be alone.

1005
01:20:44,520 --> 01:20:45,520
Eddie?

1006
01:20:52,960 --> 01:20:53,960
Open up!

1007
01:21:12,520 --> 01:21:13,840
Do you want to eat something?

1008
01:21:14,280 --> 01:21:15,200
Mm.

1009
01:21:15,920 --> 01:21:16,920
No food.

1010
01:21:17,880 --> 01:21:20,280
I'll prepare something and then I have
to go. Okay?

1011
01:21:21,720 --> 01:21:23,400
Dad comes back tomorrow morning.

1012
01:21:26,160 --> 01:21:27,360
You look beautiful.

1013
01:21:31,240 --> 01:21:32,480
Call me anytime.

1014
01:21:45,480 --> 01:21:48,400
Look, I filmed this in the clinic.

1015
01:21:56,120 --> 01:21:57,080
What is that?

1016
01:21:58,840 --> 01:21:59,760
Look.

1017
01:22:03,800 --> 01:22:05,520
He is also paraplegic?

1018
01:22:13,920 --> 01:22:15,360
Imagine...

1019
01:22:40,280 --> 01:22:42,800
Who are you trying to
prove something to?

1020
01:22:44,520 --> 01:22:46,080
I'm only trying to help.

1021
01:22:47,760 --> 01:22:49,560
You all let her down.

1022
01:22:49,720 --> 01:22:51,040
What did you just say?

1023
01:22:53,160 --> 01:22:55,160
Who do you think you are?

1024
01:22:56,520 --> 01:22:58,480
You know nothing about our live.

1025
01:22:59,280 --> 01:23:00,200
Nothing.

1026
01:23:03,120 --> 01:23:04,400
Just leave us alone.

1027
01:23:09,320 --> 01:23:10,560
This family...

1028
01:23:11,960 --> 01:23:13,080
treats her...

1029
01:23:16,240 --> 01:23:18,200
They gave up already.

1030
01:23:23,480 --> 01:23:26,080
And they treat me like
I'm the bad guy.

1031
01:23:30,400 --> 01:23:31,960
Like the bad guy...

1032
01:23:32,120 --> 01:23:33,120
<i>The bad guy?
Why?</i>

1033
01:23:33,280 --> 01:23:36,600
Why?
Maybe because they are so arrogant.

1034
01:23:40,120 --> 01:23:45,680
They feel guilty because they have
already given up on her.

1035
01:23:48,160 --> 01:23:49,360
<i>And you want to stay?</i>

1036
01:23:49,720 --> 01:23:51,640
Mum, the girl only has me.

1037
01:23:53,680 --> 01:23:56,160
She needs me.
Nobody believes in her.

1038
01:23:56,320 --> 01:23:57,440
Only I.

1039
01:23:58,000 --> 01:23:59,960
This girl only has me.

1040
01:24:00,720 --> 01:24:01,720
<i>And what about work?</i>

1041
01:24:01,880 --> 01:24:02,960
About work?

1042
01:24:03,840 --> 01:24:04,760
What?

1043
01:24:08,600 --> 01:24:11,120
I just don't want you to
get your hopes up.

1044
01:24:11,280 --> 01:24:12,720
Are you for real?

1045
01:24:14,600 --> 01:24:17,280
How do you want to achieve anything
with such an attitude?

1046
01:24:17,960 --> 01:24:20,600
- Where do you get those lines from?
- Don't talk to him like that.

1047
01:24:20,760 --> 01:24:21,880
How do I talk?

1048
01:24:22,040 --> 01:24:23,520
As if he was stupid.

1049
01:24:23,680 --> 01:24:26,160
He's not exactly a doctor, is he?

1050
01:24:26,320 --> 01:24:27,400
Well, are you one?

1051
01:24:27,560 --> 01:24:29,640
Me? No.
I'm not a doctor.

1052
01:24:30,520 --> 01:24:33,680
But I have spoken to all the leading
neurologists in this field.

1053
01:24:33,840 --> 01:24:35,880
And they all happened to tell
me the same thing.

1054
01:24:36,040 --> 01:24:37,560
- All of them!
- Ah.

1055
01:24:38,240 --> 01:24:39,680
Eddie...
Sorry!

1056
01:24:40,120 --> 01:24:41,040
Ahh.

1057
01:24:43,840 --> 01:24:45,440
Did you just feel that?

1058
01:24:46,520 --> 01:24:47,800
I think so.

1059
01:24:49,960 --> 01:24:53,280
Yes!
A little, light sting.

1060
01:24:54,520 --> 01:24:56,760
And that?
Do you feel that too?

1061
01:24:56,920 --> 01:24:57,840
No.

1062
01:24:58,160 --> 01:25:00,680
- Okay, but you just felt something.
- Yes!

1063
01:25:02,280 --> 01:25:03,200
Yes!

1064
01:25:03,480 --> 01:25:04,400
Okay.

1065
01:25:04,880 --> 01:25:07,080
- 20%...
- How is that possible?

1066
01:25:07,240 --> 01:25:08,160
20%!

1067
01:25:33,160 --> 01:25:34,800
- Ms. Schwartz.
- Hello.

1068
01:25:35,080 --> 01:25:36,080
Hello.

1069
01:25:38,920 --> 01:25:40,040
How are you?

1070
01:25:40,200 --> 01:25:42,840
That depends on what you are
about to tell me now.

1071
01:25:44,920 --> 01:25:47,360
Unfortunately, I don't have any
good news for you.

1072
01:25:48,280 --> 01:25:51,080
The therapy did not work as we hoped.

1073
01:25:51,600 --> 01:25:52,760
That cannot be.

1074
01:25:53,320 --> 01:25:55,640
I felt something in my
legs this morning.

1075
01:25:58,120 --> 01:26:00,480
That can't be related to the therapy.

1076
01:26:00,640 --> 01:26:03,200
Your body did not accept
the stem cells.

1077
01:26:04,520 --> 01:26:06,080
What is your plan now?

1078
01:26:06,880 --> 01:26:08,200
What do you suggest?

1079
01:26:08,360 --> 01:26:11,400
For now you should try to recover from
the exhausting therapy.

1080
01:26:11,760 --> 01:26:13,520
I'll simply take more of
those blockers.

1081
01:26:13,680 --> 01:26:16,040
Could her body still accept
the stem cells?

1082
01:26:18,920 --> 01:26:21,440
How did you react to the pills so far?

1083
01:26:24,080 --> 01:26:25,640
She is tough.

1084
01:26:28,360 --> 01:26:31,200
First you have to gain
your strength back.

1085
01:26:31,360 --> 01:26:33,520
So you're just giving up on me?

1086
01:26:38,320 --> 01:26:40,600
We'll take another pack
of the blockers.

1087
01:26:51,360 --> 01:26:52,880
I'm done Isaac.

1088
01:26:57,320 --> 01:26:58,720
You heard the doctor.

1089
01:27:00,000 --> 01:27:03,000
You just need to take a little bit
more of those blockers.

1090
01:27:03,320 --> 01:27:05,640
Your body can still accept
the stem cells.

1091
01:27:08,120 --> 01:27:09,880
It's pointless.

1092
01:27:10,320 --> 01:27:13,440
You are so naive.
You are so naive sometimes.

1093
01:27:19,760 --> 01:27:22,040
What kind of shitty
mentality is that?!

1094
01:27:28,040 --> 01:27:30,080
I thought you were a fighter.

1095
01:27:32,520 --> 01:27:35,320
Show them what you're made of.

1096
01:27:48,560 --> 01:27:49,600
Who is that?

1097
01:27:50,320 --> 01:27:51,240
Dad.

1098
01:27:53,680 --> 01:27:55,120
Mute him.

1099
01:27:58,920 --> 01:27:59,840
Hey!

1100
01:28:03,600 --> 01:28:06,080
You know what he's going
to say anyways.

1101
01:28:39,840 --> 01:28:42,240
Shit.
Shit!

1102
01:28:43,680 --> 01:28:45,200
Did they see us?

1103
01:28:46,280 --> 01:28:47,440
What's going on?

1104
01:28:48,200 --> 01:28:50,400
I was absent from duty
without authorization.

1105
01:28:51,400 --> 01:28:52,880
What does that mean?

1106
01:28:53,240 --> 01:28:54,920
That I'm fucked.

1107
01:29:05,720 --> 01:29:06,800
Are they following us?

1108
01:29:07,080 --> 01:29:08,240
- Sorry.
- Fuck!

1109
01:29:08,920 --> 01:29:09,840
Sorry.

1110
01:29:17,040 --> 01:29:18,000
Shit.

1111
01:29:26,240 --> 01:29:27,160
Okay.

1112
01:29:29,120 --> 01:29:32,920
Here are the tablets and a bucket in
case you have to throw up again.

1113
01:29:39,480 --> 01:29:41,840
I have to go and solve this
thing with the army.

1114
01:29:43,000 --> 01:29:43,920
Mhm.

1115
01:30:20,040 --> 01:30:21,240
What are you doing here?

1116
01:30:22,040 --> 01:30:24,080
- They're looking for you everywhere.
- I know.

1117
01:30:25,560 --> 01:30:26,720
What's wrong with you?

1118
01:30:26,880 --> 01:30:27,920
Dude, Edith is not feeling well.

1119
01:30:28,640 --> 01:30:29,560
Move. Move.

1120
01:30:34,600 --> 01:30:35,560
Where is Edith?

1121
01:30:35,720 --> 01:30:37,760
- She just laid down to rest.
- Why aren't you answering the phone?

1122
01:30:37,920 --> 01:30:38,960
Everything is under control.

1123
01:30:39,120 --> 01:30:40,600
How is she?
What did the doctor say?

1124
01:30:40,880 --> 01:30:42,720
We have to keep going a bit.

1125
01:30:42,880 --> 01:30:44,520
Just a bit longer.
There hasn't been a breakthrough yet,

1126
01:30:44,680 --> 01:30:45,720
but...

1127
01:30:45,880 --> 01:30:48,840
- Every day this will get worse!
- Man, just shut up!

1128
01:30:55,720 --> 01:30:56,640
Edith!

1129
01:31:00,600 --> 01:31:01,680
Spit it out!

1130
01:31:01,840 --> 01:31:02,760
Edith.

1131
01:31:05,680 --> 01:31:06,600
Shit.

1132
01:31:58,160 --> 01:31:59,400
I am such a fuck-up.

1133
01:31:59,840 --> 01:32:00,760
Here.

1134
01:32:01,800 --> 01:32:03,320
Sleep a bit.

1135
01:33:17,560 --> 01:33:19,080
Mr. Schwartz!
Wait!

1136
01:33:54,760 --> 01:33:56,720
- Hello Isaac.
- How is Edith?

1137
01:33:58,720 --> 01:33:59,840
She was lucky.

1138
01:34:06,360 --> 01:34:08,000
Okay.
Can I go see her?

1139
01:34:08,720 --> 01:34:09,920
She needs to rest.

1140
01:34:10,840 --> 01:34:11,840
Okay.

1141
01:34:13,600 --> 01:34:15,240
Then I'll come back later.

1142
01:34:15,720 --> 01:34:17,280
No, that's not possible.

1143
01:34:18,800 --> 01:34:19,720
Why not?

1144
01:34:21,520 --> 01:34:23,680
She doesn't want to see
you anymore Isaac.

1145
01:34:29,200 --> 01:34:30,400
She said that?

1146
01:34:31,520 --> 01:34:32,440
Yes.

1147
01:34:38,040 --> 01:34:39,400
Mr. Schwartz, please.

1148
01:34:48,480 --> 01:34:49,720
I have to see her.

1149
01:34:52,520 --> 01:34:54,320
I don't have anything else.

1150
01:34:56,400 --> 01:34:58,040
Please.
I love Edith.

1151
01:35:16,200 --> 01:35:17,120
Hi.

1152
01:35:25,800 --> 01:35:27,560
That was quite something...

1153
01:35:31,280 --> 01:35:33,400
I thought a lot, helps a lot.

1154
01:35:35,560 --> 01:35:37,800
I shouldn't have pushed you like that.

1155
01:35:37,960 --> 01:35:40,040
Isaac, I won't be able to walk again.

1156
01:35:41,160 --> 01:35:43,280
Not tomorrow, not the day
after tomorrow.

1157
01:35:45,000 --> 01:35:47,280
If you want to stop the therapy, we
will stop it immediately.

1158
01:35:48,000 --> 01:35:49,200
Done. Okay?

1159
01:35:49,360 --> 01:35:50,280
Done.

1160
01:35:51,480 --> 01:35:53,240
You don't have to do that.

1161
01:35:54,640 --> 01:35:55,840
What are you saying?

1162
01:35:56,840 --> 01:35:58,840
Edith, I love you.

1163
01:36:07,720 --> 01:36:08,960
Will you marry me?

1164
01:36:11,160 --> 01:36:12,240
I'm serious.

1165
01:36:14,160 --> 01:36:15,720
As soon as you feel better,

1166
01:36:15,880 --> 01:36:18,000
we'll go to the jeweller
and I'll buy you a ring.

1167
01:36:20,520 --> 01:36:23,200
You've spent all your money
on the therapy.

1168
01:36:23,920 --> 01:36:27,080
If we don't make the second round,
I'll still have enough.

1169
01:36:28,960 --> 01:36:31,920
You might have to make
a few compromises.

1170
01:36:32,560 --> 01:36:34,240
Maybe it will only be a small one.

1171
01:36:35,680 --> 01:36:37,000
The apartment we will be able to
afford in the beginning

1172
01:36:37,160 --> 01:36:38,640
won't be that big either, but

1173
01:36:38,800 --> 01:36:40,720
I'm going to open the
motorcycle store.

1174
01:36:43,600 --> 01:36:44,760
You can write a book.

1175
01:36:46,240 --> 01:36:48,080
You have so much to tell.

1176
01:36:49,200 --> 01:36:51,880
And with this money we will
buy a house in Italy.

1177
01:36:55,960 --> 01:36:57,720
I have a visitor.

1178
01:37:01,520 --> 01:37:02,440
Okay.

1179
01:37:02,960 --> 01:37:04,600
You'd better go now.

1180
01:37:05,960 --> 01:37:07,680
Did I say something wrong?

1181
01:37:54,040 --> 01:37:55,800
Yes, I'm looking forward too...

1182
01:37:59,160 --> 01:38:01,920
Let's see, I think she
still has a visitor.

1183
01:38:04,720 --> 01:38:05,640
Where is Isaac?

1184
01:38:06,200 --> 01:38:07,400
Gone.

1185
01:38:07,560 --> 01:38:08,480
Ok.

1186
01:38:08,760 --> 01:38:10,200
Was he just here?